{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon","id":1105543,"title":"Could I get some people to poke holes in my Head-Canon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-19T16:10:08-07:00","id":1105543,"title":"Could I get some people to poke holes in my Head-Canon?","content":"SO, I'll admit I'm a bit of a latecomer to mage. And while I've somewhat voraciously torn into the setting there are some books I don't have, and some knowledge about the setting I simply lack. For example? Voormas's Exploits. I know some of what happened but fairly little.<br /> <br /> Anyway, My Head-Canon largely relies on a couple simple things.<br /> <br /> 1.) The Anthropic Principle/Subjective Reality.<br /> <br /> For this Head-Canon to work, Reality must fundamentally be determined by what people believe. There cannot be any deeper secret of 'how reality works' than 'this is what people believe and so it's true.' This one is fairly easily justified, given the setting as a whole. Everyone is a mage, just not everyone is aware of it.<br /> <br /> 2.) Extra-Temporality.<br /> <br /> Time. It's a bit of a murky sphere for obvious reasons. But this whole bit of thinking is dependent on the fact that time is much like space. Things that existed in the past exist still. Just somewhere else. This one is a bit harder to justify, but ties in with the above.<br /> <br /> 3.) Mages can, to a degree, subvert the Anthropic Principle.<br /> <br /> Again, basic bit of the setting. Mages reject the reality created by the masses and form their own. Allowing them to steer reality if their vision is compelling enough to the sleepers.<br /> <br /> <br /> In essence, the idea is, that in the past. Humans were scattered. Separate. They came up with many different beliefs about the world, and accordingly, the world accommodated them due to the Anthropic Principle. The wilderness's were vast, terrible and full of monsters because that's what people thought they were. Some people awoke to the idea that things didn't have to be this way. First they made simple things. You could move thoughts from one mans head to another, by using noises. If you rub sticks together it makes fire and fire can fight off monsters. Etc Etc.<br /> <br /> These people grow old and die, and their children carry on. Maybe making up new things. Maybe disregarding what their parents believed entirely. <i>But the consensus still includes their parents.</i> The Consensus is not bound by time. And while parts of it are malleable, the 'universal constants' are those things that mankind has known to be true for time immemorial. The oldest ideas don't just rely upon the mystical might of those living today, but <i>the force of every avatar of every person who has believed that idea from the dawn of time.</i> This is why Spirits exist, why they have powers outside the modern consensus. Because animism is one of the oldest faiths of mankind. Spirits literally have untold billions of sleeping avatars behind them. Believing, &quot;Yes, they exist. Yes, they can do this.&quot; This is why the Historical Constant exists. Because if you attempt to change the past, you are getting hit by EVERY SINGLE PERSON WHO'S LIFE WOULD BE CHANGED. Even unobtrusive things, You say &quot;I want to be in the corner store on January 1st, 1944&quot; Everyone who was there is smacking you with a counterspell every time they remember that moment for the rest of their lives and remember you not being there.<br /> <br /> And this also shows WHY the Technocracy is so hell bent on controlling the information of the masses rather than simply wiping out the magical community. If the Historical Constant is the weight of the forgotten dead trillions holding up the old ways. That means If the Technocracy can control the future generations, eventually they will have their consensus gain power to break it. Gaining the ability to rewrite the dawn of time. Compared to that, killing one more hermetic is incidental. If they want to play with their toys and snap up a random eccentric here or there, that's overall, ok. Technocratic control of the modern consensus on the other hand.... that's the cornerstone of their strategy. If they lose that the game is lost.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense? Or am I overthinking this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T17:09:43-07:00","id":1105551,"title":"","content":"Hoo boy. Well, for starters, the standard disclaimer, my statements don't reflect the opinions of the BBC, you are free to do what you want &amp;c. &amp;c.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon#post1105543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, My Head-Canon largely relies on a couple simple things...</div> </div> </div> </div>I will note that your 1.) does not seem to generally hold; look at Book of Mirrors, origMadness, etc. I feel Revised's excellent definition of paradigm accommodates the distinction better than most.<br /> <br /> Leaving aside my disagreement about a fundamental premise, if 2.) holds, why would we presume that the avatars of past people - which have reincarnated - can effectively work against themselves? If new avatars are being created as more people are born than previously existed, surely the future holds more new Avatars than the past? Once you have ten humans, don't they override the first two by strength of numbers (even if two of their Avatars are divided in their purpose)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T17:18:19-07:00","id":1105554,"title":"","content":"Because you can hang effects with time. If you view that as, rather than putting the effect in a box to take out later, targeting a point in the future, then that makes sense. The magic already happened.<br /> <br /> If you spend several lifetimes building something up. Ensuring it can withstand the weight of time, Can you bring it all crashing down in an instant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T17:24:41-07:00","id":1105556,"title":"","content":"Sure, if (several+) of my future incarnations tear it down. If time is simultaneous, my future selves have already spent the entirety of the future undoing what I have/will/am done/do/doing. Instant and lifetime are meaningless measures.<br /> <br /> If we're being targeted by Time-shifted effects from the past, can I use Time 2 warding to alleviate the Historical Constant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T17:27:20-07:00","id":1105557,"title":"","content":"But the future isn't set, now is it? You're assuming the future is one set thing, like the past is one set thing. Could you? Theoretically yes. You'd need a hell of a power source to back that up though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T17:36:02-07:00","id":1105558,"title":"","content":"If the future isn't a set place, it's remarkable good fortune that my past selves managed to target the right one with their Time 4.<br /> <br /> Can I use Entropy/Time to baffle and break the Historical Constant by rerouting the past's inhabitants targeting into potential futures that will not be realized?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T20:57:15-07:00","id":1105586,"title":"","content":"I don't really like the pure Subjective Reality approach, as it has far too many holes in it: what was reality like before man came along? Why did the first men expect the world to be vast and harsh wilderness? Etc. That said, I'm with you on Time magic: the Consensus can extend its influence through space and time and even into the spirit world; but it's limited by the same sorts of barriers that limit the Awakened: Correspondence ranges mean that the Consensus tends to divide up into Reality Zones; the Gauntlet generally shields the Umbra from the Consensus; and the fact that Time magic has an easier time reaching into the future than into the past means that our ancestors have a lot more say on what or world is like than our descendants do. It also allows the relatively small population from the past to have more of an influence on us than our much larger population in the present has on them.<br /> <br /> For more on this, see my thoughts about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\">the nature of the Consensus</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-20-2017, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T22:11:02-07:00","id":1105599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the fact that Time magic has an easier time reaching into the future than into the past means that our ancestors have a lot more say on what or world is like than our descendants do. It also allows the relatively small population from the past to have more of an influence on us than our much larger population in the present has on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Digging deeper on that, if every universal constant it's based on subjectivity, and magick has a harder time affecting the past than the future because Historical Inertia, then this &quot;restriction&quot; has to be consensual too.<br /> <br /> This leads you to a dilema: If the past it's harder to affect than the future, in spite of people in the future being much more numerous, and it's the people of the future, not the past, that has the biggest potential influence on the limitations embeded into the timeless Consensus without setting any restriction, including the so called *fact* that it's easier to affect the future than the past, then they, the people of the future, had to leave their own beliefs aside to favor those of the people in the past in order to set that restriction on their own timeless influece. Isn't that weird?<br /> <br /> I think we may be able to explain this as a natural quirk of human mind that makes us believe in the past with as much strenght as we believe in the present or more. We build our beliefs whith what was teached to us, and thus we have a natural tendency to believe in our history...which, of course, comes with the next dilema: If human mind has certain &quot;natural&quot; quirks, then are these created by the Consensus (from the future, because there is no past at this point), or the human nature exists as something that was set before the Consensus, and thus isn't subjective?. If it's the former, then we can't solve the Time dilema this way, if it's the latter, then there are constants that transcends the Consensus (at least with regards to human nature)<br /> <br /> Personaly. I prefer a world with a few Constants outside the Consensus (and I think this it's better supported in the material), but I don't think your theory it's bad, Enginseer. I like the part of Consensus being atemporal, even with all the problems it causes. It's creative and isn't quite in the books, but it's feasible taking in count what magick can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-20-2017, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T22:50:01-07:00","id":1105607,"title":"","content":"To clarify one point, my default assumption is that \u201cConsensus\u201d is what <i>humans</i> believe: if you have an Avatar, even a Slumbering one, you contribute to the Consensus; and other than those who have had their Avatars destroyed (e.g., Gilgul or the Embrace), all humans have Avatars. Meanwhile, if you're <i>not</i> human, you probably <i>don't</i> have an Avatar \u2014 though the Chorister notion of the Pure Ones and the One suggests the possibility that the higher ranks of the spirit hierarchy might effectively <i>be</i> Avatars. <br /> <br /> Which gives a \u201csubjective reality loophole\u201d by implying that what Constants and ground rules there are might be the result of God or Gaia or the Triat, etc. exerting His/Her/Its/Their Will on the cosmos. It's not an explanation that the Void Engineers would approve of; but there you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T23:50:06-07:00","id":1105622,"title":"","content":"All of this philosophy inspired me to create a theory of my own...it takes the things to a more, let's say &quot;mystical&quot;, and less subjective, perspective, but I will leave it anyway:<br /> <br /> We tend to think about time in terms of past, present,and future. But in truth we colapse time in past and future. Present it's just an instant, and in the argument of who pulls stronger, past or future, that small middle ground it's negelgible.<br /> <br /> However, the common binary conception of time it's not the only way to think this concept. Greeks had three different words for time. Our conception of time as a river that flows from past to the future (or it's the other way arround?) was understood with the word Cronos. Kairos and Aeon where the other two words that meant time, pertaining to very different concepts. I will concentrate on <b>Aion</b>.<br /> <br /> Aion, it's something like what we call eternity. But eternity in the sense of Aion it's not an endless amount of time, nor does it references the infinite space/time continuum-all of that it's Cronos.<br /> <br /> Aion it's eternity understood as something that exists, litaraly, outside time. As such, Aion it's simultaneous, and foraneous, to all Time and everything that implies. it's the true &quot;Correspondence Point&quot; for Time. Plato went so far as to say that Time(Cronos) it's but a shadow of Aion.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Now, keeping that in mind, let's begin:</i></b><br /> <br /> Imagine that Magick, the Consensus, and thus (in a way) Avatars exist trully outside, above, and beyond, Time. This actually seems plausible, after all, you can't &quot;ascelerate&quot; your magick with Time (magick tend to follow esoteric rules that transcend Time to an extent).<br /> <br /> Imagine the Consensus as something that it's simultaneous to ALL TIME. This is even compatible with the multiple timelines and &quot;not written future&quot; theory, because eternity can easily encompas every possible timeline, even if these are strictly infinite...<br /> This Consensus of all Humanity compressed in less than an instant, abarcating the whole of Time, the Consensus Beyond Time it's something indistinguishable from THE ONE. Past, present, future, all are one in <s>Yog-Sothoth</s> the Consensus <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Consensus exists outside time, and being outside time the People agreed with itself on the basic rules. In a way you could say that the Consensus of the &quot;future people&quot; sat to talk with the Consensus of &quot;past people&quot; leaving their guises and treating each one as an equal part of everything-not before time, but outside time-and ageed on certain things.<br /> <br /> They agreed on the concepts of Time and Space as we understand them (time flows from the past to the future), among other things like the existence of Prime and the human nature (and the nature of the spirits if you want to include them as part of the Consensus).<br /> <br /> It's not that an alien created the rules (in spite of previous jokes, that's not exactly my proposal). My idea it's that the cero-sum of everything that the People can possibly conceive in all eternity created the rules. The sum of all human belief as could only be seen by an hipotetical someone that exists outside time and can see the belief that every being held at every potential era will determine if the time has to flow from the past to the future, if the future isn't written, etc.<br /> <br /> In setting the rules, the Eternal Consensus fragmentation was the only logical conclusion. The existence that outside time it's compresed into eternity and absolute power it's the multiplicity that exists within the flow of time and space.<br /> It's not that the One &quot;died&quot; to create the universe, but rather than the One it's just the sum of the belief of untold beings understood as something that that transcends Time, and thus can interact with it from the perspective of someone that can see the beguining and the end of Time. The &quot;fragmentation of the One&quot; it's an apt methapor to understand that the One and the Multiple are the same.<br /> <br /> If you want the future to be uncertain, no problem, because, as I said, the Eternal Consensus can easily colapse into infinite potential universes that may or may not become part of the current wheel of time, but &quot;exist&quot; as &quot;what ifs&quot; (that can be explored as Everet Volumes).<br /> <br /> This theory agrees in the idea that the Consensus created everything, but a few things where created from a point that's outside time and outside the individual egos of singular people, like the human nature, and thus won't be overriden (unless they were meant to be). They're &quot;Consensual&quot; in a sense that's far beyond the power of any mage faction to manipulate. Maybe with Time and Prime Archspheres at 9-10 (or the all mighty 6) a mage could start to understand it's enormity, and what would be necessary to manipulate it (if possible)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-20-2017, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T01:39:24-07:00","id":1105634,"title":"","content":"I am a fan of reality zones and the previous incarnation, the reality bubbles.<br /> <br /> If the reality/consensus changes, then it changes the past, the future and generally everything <b>within</b> said zone/bubble. But the beings in the past have their own bubble, and so remain largely unaltered.<br /> I leave the cosmological constants and historical inertia largely undefined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T06:12:36-07:00","id":1105663,"title":"","content":"Which aspect of your head canon are you looking for holes in and how detailed do you want them? I think overall you have a workable system, but the there's a lot that could trip you up if you or your players get into the details.<br /> <br /> For instance, here is a question: What happens to someone from the future visiting the present?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:19:25-07:00","id":1105795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1105586#post1105586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really like the pure Subjective Reality approach, as it has far too many holes in it: what was reality like before man came along? Why did the first men expect the world to be vast and harsh wilderness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the question was addresed many times over the years. What was really like before man came ? Everything. Demons explain that before the Hammer of Consensus fall on the Tellurian, everything existed at once. It's stronger that reality being subjective. If I do not mistake, subjective reality states that reality is what you think it is. It involves the coexistence of all paradigms, meaning that all paradigms can become reality if the local Will is strong enough (hence reality zones, etc.). Before the apparition of the Consensus everything just was. It means that every paradigm was simultaneously true. That's the way The Fallen describe it. And at the begining, there was the original Entity. It was the One, it was the Big Bang, it was the Grand Engineer, it was Unity, it was everything. At that moment, Time fit simultaneously all your definitions. The Consensus fixed the Arrow of Time when men got Avatars, shards of the Entity.<br /> I do not totally agree with you and I see no loopholes in that theory. It accredites all theories really. Could you precise please. I woud like to see what I'm missing in your statement.<br /> Concerning your second point, I do not think men just expected something of reality. Reality was shaped bu their will as their hold fragments of the original Entity. It took eons to make it the way it currently is.<br /> <br /> Concerning the flow of Time, Mage: The Ascension addressed it to in several books and in a way close to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>'s theory. The Consensus created the Arrow of Time when Time was at the same time guided and eternal. It was a solution chosen by the Consensus to make easier the understanding of the Tellurian by men. As an exemple of a reality existing beyound all perceptions, Batini (see Lost Paths) say that they follow the Doctrine of Unity explained to them at their rebirth by a cosmic entity named Entelechy, which appearance echoed in all times, future and past at the same time. That moment is even central in the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:33:52-07:00","id":1105803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1105663#post1105663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which aspect of your head canon are you looking for holes in and how detailed do you want them? I think overall you have a workable system, but the there's a lot that could trip you up if you or your players get into the details.<br /> <br /> For instance, here is a question: What happens to someone from the future visiting the present?</div> </div> </div> </div>What happens to you visiting the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T13:51:11-07:00","id":1105834,"title":"","content":"The real issue here is that you have to be down with subjective reality. And in order to be down with that, you have to be down with information spontaneously generously generating itself and non-causal reality. Seriously, for reals. If you're not down with entirely unexplained phenomena, which provides the escape valve for the metaphysic of magick, then Mage The Awakening is really your game, because what you really want is a first principle, which goes entirely against a game in which belief, and only belief and will, determines reality. Objective reality must be abandoned on all levels. Really, it has to be. <br /> <br /> This is what really irks the shit out of some gamers, who otherwise love Mage but desperately snuffle and root around the setting for a first cause or impose outside metaphysics (like Werewolf's Triat) into Mage. Seriously, ya need to let go, and submerse yourself in things like esoteric Buddhism which regards all phenomenologically perception as inherently temporary. It's existensialism taken to 11. You won't ever get the objective first cause that some gamers desperately crave. It's terrible, horrid, beautiful, super scary freedom.<br /> <br /> I love Ascension because of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T13:53:11-07:00","id":1105835,"title":"","content":"A great guide to non-causal time and ideas - Aetherco's Continuum. This game, a great RPG in and of itself. also made me a better Mage player. The setting of Continuum is one of 'Information is All', which is identical to Mage (although Continuum's setting has different physical laws, obviously.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T13:54:12-07:00","id":1105836,"title":"","content":"For Time Sphere, you can also crib the guidelines from Mage: The Awakening's Time Arcana, which lets you do actual time travel and is gameable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T16:58:25-07:00","id":1105871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1105803#post1105803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happens to you visiting the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so it's the same whether the time traveler is from the future or the present. The future memories of people existing today will inflict paradox if a time traveler shows up somewhere they don't remember him being.<br /> <br /> All good so far, but let's take time travel out of the equation for a moment. Let's say a mage from today is hungry and is trying to decide whether to go to a pub or a pizzeria. The future memories of people existing today will include which one he goes to. Is his choice already made? Will he get Paradox if he goes against those future memories? Can you get Paradox for a completely mundane decision?<br /> <br /> Strange, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T22:43:13-07:00","id":1105952,"title":"","content":"This is going way too far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I use time travel as a theme of one of my campaigns but collides two moments far distant, the first being in a time before paradox comes. That last point helps.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I tend to consider that the existence of the Consensus out of time is somewhat mystical. I do not think that the choice of the kind of pizza you eat falls into that category ^^ in the physical part of the tellurian, the Arrow of time defines what is past, present and future. No paradox if you make a &quot;mistake&quot; when you eat pizza <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T00:35:10-07:00","id":1105971,"title":"","content":"Nice idea for a Time induced Quiet.<br /> <br /> You are constantly worried if you do the right things. And life in constant fear of the Time Paradox you could create by eating pizza instead of a club sandwich...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T05:29:35-07:00","id":1106012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1105952#post1105952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going way too far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I use time travel as a theme of one of my campaigns but collides two moments far distant, the first being in a time before paradox comes. That last point helps.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I tend to consider that the existence of the Consensus out of time is somewhat mystical. I do not think that the choice of the kind of pizza you eat falls into that category ^^ in the physical part of the tellurian, the Arrow of time defines what is past, present and future. No paradox if you make a &quot;mistake&quot; when you eat pizza <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, hey, hey, on the way to the pizzeria you might actually step on a butterfly you would have left alone if you'd gone to the pub. And we all know what butterflies do to the timeline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To be clear, I only chose pizza because it was in line with the original example of a time traveler in a corner store. It's possible to use more meaningful actions in both the time travel and mundane examples if that better underscores the issues. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T05:39:54-07:00","id":1106015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106012#post1106012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, hey, hey, on the way to the pizzeria you might actually step on a butterfly you would have left alone if you'd gone to the pub. And we all know what butterflies do to the timeline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To be clear, I only chose pizza because it was in line with the original example of a time traveler in a corner store. It's possible to use more meaningful actions in both the time travel and mundane examples if that better underscores the issues. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I totally understood your point and just went on with your exemple. What I meant is that you could do many things without that kind of backlash. My opinion is that only highly mystical or spiritual feats should lead to the Consensus reacting from all time points. <br /> <br /> That said, it brings a question. What about the gilgul? It really prevents the avatar to come back doesn't it? Well... That's a problem don't you think? Or that means that the victim had no choice and that he is cut off from his avatar in all the possible time lines...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:34:23-07:00","id":1106099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106012#post1106012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, hey, hey, on the way to the pizzeria you might actually step on a butterfly you would have left alone if you'd gone to the pub. And we all know what butterflies do to the timeline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Stupid butterflies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:15:49-07:00","id":1106120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, hey, hey, on the way to the pizzeria you might actually step on a butterfly you would have left alone if you'd gone to the pub. And we all know what butterflies do to the timeline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that butterfly you stepped upon was the sight that would give hope to someone that was going to suicide. If that someone commited suicide, it would prevent the born of a boy that would Awaken, Master the Time Sphere, and go to the past, where he would make the Nazi win the War. And so, because you wanted to eat pizza, we now live in Naziland (as happens in so many timelines)...I imagine that this it's what Time Masters tell other mages to convince them where to eat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> From the PoV of my theory, however, I've thought about that dilema. I think there's a solution, if we use multiverse theory.<br /> <br /> The Consensus out of time knows all possible outcomes of all posible timelines, but not what's going to enter in the axis of time.<br /> <br /> The Consensus out of time it's like a guy offering you a mirriad of universes and posibilities that he tought &quot;possible&quot;. He knows all the potential outcomes of each and every one of these strands, but he doesn't know what you are going to choose in the end. This way, he can define the rules that all the timelines are going to obey (even to the point of changing the rules here or there), but doesn't care about what, of the mirriad of choices, it's going to be selected by YOU (having free will) to be part of your timeline.<br /> <br /> This way, you don't have to worry about creating The Mother of All Paradoxes by stepping on the wrong butterfly-which doesn't mean that you won't have to worry about Nazis ruling the world as consequence (the Consensus Beyond Time doesn't worry about that, but you certainly should). <hr />In a more general note, the easier way to solve all temporal paradoxes it's to say that stepping on butterflies generates alternate timelines, and that a time traveler from the future comes from a time that it's potential in it's very nature.<br /> <br /> Only problem with this theory it's that it's boring because you can't change the future by changing the past (you merely create a new variant)...I think it would be more interesting if we allow for a way to alter one's own timeline, because this is a good plot hock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-21-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:27:44-07:00","id":1106126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real issue here is that you have to be down with subjective reality. And in order to be down with that, you have to be down with information spontaneously generously generating itself and non-causal reality. Seriously, for reals. If you're not down with entirely unexplained phenomena, which provides the escape valve for the metaphysic of magick, then Mage The Awakening is really your game, because what you really want is a first principle, which goes entirely against a game in which belief, and only belief and will, determines reality. Objective reality must be abandoned on all levels. Really, it has to be.<br /> <br /> This is what really irks the shit out of some gamers, who otherwise love Mage but desperately snuffle and root around the setting for a first cause or impose outside metaphysics (like Werewolf's Triat) into Mage. Seriously, ya need to let go</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm...the One and the Pure Ones (Mage-from the very first edition and never leaved) would like to disagree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T10:46:30-07:00","id":1106139,"title":"","content":"What happens when two or more groups of Sleepers disagree on the basic nature of reality under this framework? How many Sleepers do you need to have on your side before you can shape local Reality? What keeps suicidal Sleepers from simply dying in their sleep? <br /> <br /> The problem with Subjective Reality is that it is often a reality of victimization and exploitation. For example, take a look at the US before the Civil War. The dominant paradigm was that African-Americans were subhumans who deserved slavery because of the supposed Curse of Ham. Since the vast majority of whites across the US (meaning the majority of the population of the US before the 1940s) believed that African Americans were subhuman until before the 1940s, you run into a real squicky situation (World War II changed a lot of opinions and was one of the reasons for the success of Civil Rights during the 1960s). <br /> <br /> The same thing could be applied to any disadvantaged group since their disadvantaged status would be created by Subjective Reality. If Subjective Reality exists, then the majority paradigm determines Reality. If Objective Reality exists, then the majority paradigm is just an opinion. <br /> <br /> If people like bigotry, racism, sexism, etc, then they want Subjective Reality. If people do not, then they want Objective Reality. People can like Subjective Reality without being hateful, but it is usually because they do not really think through the consequences of Subjective Reality for anyone but their character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:02:05-07:00","id":1106149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106139#post1106139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Subjective Reality is that it is often a reality of victimization and exploitation...</div> </div> </div> </div>:facepalm:<br /> <br /> This is actually an interesting philosophical dilemma with Subjective Reality, albeit one most proponents realized and dealt with a <i>long</i> time ago, so I get why you'd bring into the discussion. But do you have to try poisoning the well every single time you bring it up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-21-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:41:38-07:00","id":1106178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106120#post1106120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Consensus out of time knows all possible outcomes of all posible timelines, but not what's going to enter in the axis of time.<br /> The Consensus out of time it's like a guy offering you a mirriad of universes and posibilities that he tought &quot;possible&quot;. He knows all the potential outcomes of each and every one of these strands, but he doesn't know what you are going to choose in the end. This way, he can define the rules that all the timelines are going to obey (even to the point of changing the rules here or there), but doesn't care about what, of the mirriad of choices, it's going to be selected by YOU (having free will) to be part of your timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now I disagree. The Consensus knows nothing (you know nothing Consensus). It offers nothing neither. You could say that the Consensus believes, but it fixes nothing. It's a collective will having huge inertia. It does not know the outcome of events, it <i>thinks</i> it knows the outcome of events. I do not think the Consensus is omniscient. A metaphor could be to reprensent the Consensus as a child having strong ideas about all subjects but knowing nothing of their true nature. It merely repeats what anyone tells. I do not think it exists outside of Time neither, but I believe it to live through all times, which is different, don't you think ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T11:59:20-07:00","id":1106185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">What happens when two or more groups of Sleepers disagree on the basic nature of reality under this framework? How many Sleepers do you need to have on your side before you can shape local Reality? What keeps suicidal Sleepers from simply dying in their sleep?<br /> <br /> The problem with Subjective Reality is that it is often a reality of victimization and exploitation. For example, take a look at the US before the Civil War. The dominant paradigm was that African-Americans were subhumans who deserved slavery because of the supposed Curse of Ham. Since the vast majority of whites across the US (meaning the majority of the population of the US before the 1940s) believed that African Americans were subhuman until before the 1940s, you run into a real squicky situation (World War II changed a lot of opinions and was one of the reasons for the success of Civil Rights during the 1960s).<br /> <br /> The same thing could be applied to any disadvantaged group since their disadvantaged status would be created by Subjective Reality. If Subjective Reality exists, then the majority paradigm determines Reality. If Objective Reality exists, then the majority paradigm is just an opinion.<br /> <br /> If people like bigotry, racism, sexism, etc, then they want Subjective Reality. If people do not, then they want Objective Reality. People can like Subjective Reality without being hateful, but it is usually because they do not really think through the consequences of Subjective Reality for anyone but their character.</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> XDXDXDXD<br /> <br /> I can totally imagine a new age Traditionalist arguing against Technocratic paradigmatical domination with this exact argument.<br /> <br /> But no, I disagree, there's no way Subjective Reality necessarily helps all those nasty stuff. For several reasons:<br /> <br /> 1\u00ba Reality Zones. Ghettos ain't usually frecuented by the oligarchy, and thus in places where those &quot;minories&quot; live they would be majoritary, and thus control the local Consensus. A Reality Zone can be as small as a house, or even a room, thus, for those people that have strong self-determination there will always be a place of respite of their suffering<br /> <br /> Actually, opressors, racists, and all those...want an Objective Reality...one where their theories are true. This is why they often cite &quot;science&quot; in their hate speech.<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba Because usually opressors aren't majoritary.<br /> <br /> This &quot;minority&quot; stuff that the SJW have stuck in their minds really has to stop, being part of the majority rarely means having true privileges, nor automatically makes you a victim. As an example: Woman aren't a minority, they make up the majority of the human population.<br /> <br /> Privilege usually belongs to the 1%, and they are who decide policy. Under Subjective Reality, they wouldn't be able to do this unless they manipulate the Masses to believe like them. In a Subjective Reality woman would just have to believe that they're powerful to make it happen. And the system could be subverted by just believing that an alternative it's possible<br /> <br /> Which it's all that mage it's about. mage tells us of conspirations that, being a minority, shape the Consensus to their images. There are even a few mages that want to free people, to make them realize that their destiny doesn't have to depend on the whims of a minority on the power, that the people has the power.<br /> <br /> 3\u00ba<br /> To answer your first questions: If 100 normal people entirely invested into making a ritual happen (true believers) it's needed to make a vulgar ritual Coincident, probably you need a LOT more strongly convinced people believing in something to make it not only Coincident, but also &quot;normal&quot; (altering Reality).<br /> <br /> And this altered Reality ends when you encounter a Reality Zone opposed to your Paradigm, as can be shown in the Zones where cellphones don't work. People can counter the Consensus of other people (granted, the majority can win this battle, but there needs to be a huge majority to make a total defeat. Even then it can be fought by willfull people, esp. mages, and reversed).<br /> <br /> Also, people need to &quot;really&quot; believe to make something real. Merely wanting to be dead isn't enough to magickally die (heck, not even for Mages with Arete lower than 3), you need to believe very strongly that it's going to happen.<br /> Incidentally, this kinda happens in the real world, hypochondriacs may really present symptoms of the sickness they believe that they have (I don't think one can die by believing, but getting sick comes dangerously close, for a world supposedly ruled by pure objectivity).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-21-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:23:34-07:00","id":1106196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, now I disagree. The Consensus knows nothing (you know nothing Consensus). It offers nothing neither. You could say that the Consensus believes, but it fixes nothing. It's a collective will having huge inertia. It does not know the outcome of events, it <i>thinks</i> it knows the outcome of events. I do not think the Consensus is omniscient. A metaphor could be to reprensent the Consensus as a child having strong ideas about all subjects but knowing nothing of their true nature. It merely repeats what anyone tells. I do not think it exists outside of Time neither, but I believe it to live through all times, which is different, don't you think ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that notion.<br /> <br /> I was trying to point, for my theory of a consensus out of time + multiverse (that assumes that it exists outside of time), that the Consensus beliefs are compossed with the beliefs that can be found in all of time.<br /> <br /> If a Mage with Mind 10/Time 10 would manage to feel the beliefs of every relevant being across all time and space, including alternate timelines, he would have an idea of what beliefs are held more across all timelines, who are more localized, and what beliefs are rarer. The things most commonly believed across all timelines would form the Constants for all the universe, less common beliefs may form lesser Constants or be subject to a more localized Consensus.<br /> <br /> Since belief forms the universe these big beliefs would be undeniably true (in some weird way), and thus, my hipotetical Mind/Time 10 mage (but not the Consensus) would have a vast, if not absolute, knowledge of Reality (if belief shapes reality, what's more widely believed would be truer, even if some places may defy the notion, but the mage would know this too, because the consensus outside time includes these as &quot;minoritary&quot; beliefs).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-21-2017, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:41:54-07:00","id":1106200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106149#post1106149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> :facepalm:<br /> <br /> This is actually an interesting philosophical dilemma with Subjective Reality, albeit one most proponents realized and dealt with a <i>long</i> time ago, so I get why you'd bring into the discussion. But do you have to try poisoning the well every single time you bring it up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a philosopher, the idea that the dilemmas concerning Subjective Reality have been dealt with long time ago is a fallacy. There are plenty of existing arguments against Subjective Reality that are respected within philosophy that make the arguments for Subjective Reality seem like logical Swiss cheese. But I do not think that anyone here wants to get into that argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:45:29-07:00","id":1106202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106139#post1106139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people like bigotry, racism, sexism, etc, then they want Subjective Reality. If people do not, then they want Objective Reality. People can like Subjective Reality without being hateful, but it is usually because they do not really think through the consequences of Subjective Reality for anyone but their character..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're over-simplifying the idea.<br /> <br /> Let's take, as an example, some hypothetical american town. The majority of the inhabitants of this town are white and they're racist. They believe that black and latinx people are inferior: poorly educated, criminals, et cetera.<br /> <br /> And what happens in this town is that black and latinx people are denied promotions or better paying jobs. Most end up in poorer neighborhoods, where the schools have next to no funding and incredibly outdated materials. The police profile black and latinx people and subject them to greater scrutiny. When they're arrested for crimes, they're not offered the same leniency that their white counterparts have. (That's not even getting into economic desperation as a motivation to commit a crime. Or the lack of accessibility to proper mental health treatment. And so on and so forth.)<br /> <br /> So what do you end up with? A town where many of the black and latinx people are poorly educated, and are more likely to have criminal records.<br /> <br /> And there you have it: an example of subjective reality. The black and latinx people of the town aren't inferior, of course. But because of things like institutionalized privilege and systemic racism, many of them do have those qualities that the white majority deems as &quot;inferior&quot;. If they lived somewhere else with better access to education, where racial profiling is discouraged, where the Judges and District Attorneys are more willing to treat people on an equal basis. Where these people aren't denied for jobs or promotions, and have access to mental health treatment and so on and so forth. Then these people wouldn't be &quot;poorly educated&quot; or &quot;criminals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ultimately, that's an example of a Reality Zone. It's not about somehow magically making the Curse of Ham real, it's about people, consciously or unconsciously, creating a system and environment that reinforces their own beliefs.<br /> <br /> Subjective Reality isn't however always a bad thing, though. Because when Reality is subjective, it can also be changed: Systems can be dismantled. Bigotry can be overcome. Access can be improved and insured. It's not remotely easy, but it can happen.<br /> <br /> This is why Mage practices include things like &quot;dominion&quot; and &quot;art of desire&quot;, because not everything that influences reality requires an arete roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-21-2017, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:49:58-07:00","id":1106204,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8572\" data-vbnamecard=\"8572\">NicoTheDuck</a><br /> <br /> I theorized a Consensus outside time because I needed to explain human origin in a Reality that's Consensual. If reality it's made by human mind, then where did human come from?. My answer would be: Human (or rather, human belief) has a way to transcend time, and created the conditions for human to appear &quot;naturaly&quot;. Replace human belief with spirit belief if they have a say too (wich they have, in their Umbral Realms).<br /> <br /> What would be your argument for the Consensus living inside (and thus being subject to) Time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:51:27-07:00","id":1106207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106200#post1106200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as a philosopher, the idea that the dilemmas concerning Subjective Reality have been dealt with long time ago is a fallacy. There are plenty of existing arguments against Subjective Reality that are respected within philosophy that make the arguments for Subjective Reality seem like logical Swiss cheese. But I do not think that anyone here wants to get into that argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>The proponents of Mage having a Subjective Reality, Aya. <br /> <br /> These are the Mage forums. We're in a thread talking about the metaphysics of Mage. I shouldn't have to spell out that we're not discussing the nature of the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:52:42-07:00","id":1106209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AyaTari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as a philosopher, the idea that the dilemmas concerning Subjective Reality have been dealt with long time ago is a fallacy. There are plenty of existing arguments against Subjective Reality that are respected within philosophy that make the arguments for Subjective Reality seem like logical Swiss cheese. But I do not think that anyone here wants to get into that argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a student of philosophy, I don't usually defend subjective reality in real life, but your arguments left me unconvinced that such a reality would be inherently immoral (or less moral than an objective one).<br /> <br /> Even if the concept was inherently immoral, we're talking about the World of Darkness. Reality being a douchebag doesn't detract from the theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-21-2017, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:17:37-07:00","id":1106282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106204#post1106204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8572\" data-vbnamecard=\"8572\">NicoTheDuck</a><br /> <br /> I theorized a Consensus outside time because I needed to explain human origin in a Reality that's Consensual. If reality it's made by human mind, then where did human come from?. My answer would be: Human (or rather, human belief) has a way to transcend time, and created the conditions for human to appear &quot;naturaly&quot;. Replace human belief with spirit belief if they have a say too (wich they have, in their Umbral Realms).<br /> <br /> What would be your argument for the Consensus living inside (and thus being subject to) Time?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is deep. I like it a lot. However, reality is not made by man, not in Mage anyway. It is shaped by man, or by his Will, which is completely different. Mage is a 90's game, times when post-modernism was the current fashion ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","user":"NicoTheDuck","date":". 06-21-2017, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:26:02-07:00","id":1106287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106207#post1106207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The proponents of Mage having a Subjective Reality, Aya.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speak for yourself. Or are you \u201cNo True Scotsman\u201ding me, in that I'm not really a fan of Ascension because I have my doubts about purely subjective reality?<br /> <br /> My own view on subjective reality is a bit like the old joke about statistics: 97% of all statistics, including this one, are totally worthless. In a similar way, there's no such thing as 100% subjective reality; because if everything is subjective, so is the statement that everything's subjective.<br /> <br /> This isn't just word-play: in order for the Technocracy not to be objectively wrong, there needs to be the possibility that they might be at least somewhat right. Either way, there's an objective truth here. As such, my take on it is that subjective reality isn't an objective fact; it's what the Traditions believe. It may <i>or may not</i> be true\u2605; there's no way of knowing for certain. What <i>is</i> certain is that it's a <i>useful</i> belief, because it fosters the Traditions' diverse and cooperative culture. So I have no problem with the Traditions pushing this notion, whether or not it's ultimately true.<br /> <br /> \u2605 For some value of true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106207#post1106207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are the Mage forums. We're in a thread talking about the metaphysics of Mage. I shouldn't have to spell out that we're not discussing the nature of the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div> Real-world metaphysics inform Mage metaphysics. The former are a valid topic as long as you keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> My go-to example is Climate Change: if reality really is determined by the Consensus, then a valid strategy for combatting Climate Change would be to convince the Masses that it doesn't exist. Perversely, those who warn of the danger and convince people that it's a real problem would be the ones responsible for it. So it can't be as simple as \u201creality is whatever you believe it is\u201d: belief, and will, needs to be a factor (because the Traditions can't be objectively wrong); but that can't be all there is to it.<br /> <br /> I do like Aleph's notion of a temporal counterpart to the Correspondence Point, something that exists outside of Time and defines the rules of time without being subject to them. I'm not necessarily going to say that whatever it is that imposes its Will on Time is human. That's certainly a possibility; but in keeping with my preference for subjective reality only being subjectively true, I'm not in favor of nailing down the identity of whatever inhabits Eternity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:21:05-07:00","id":1106312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My go-to example is Climate Change: if reality really is determined by the Consensus, then a valid strategy for combatting Climate Change would be to convince the Masses that it doesn't exist. Perversely, those who warn of the danger and convince people that it's a real problem would be the ones responsible for it. So it can't be as simple as \u201creality is whatever you believe it is\u201d: belief, and will, needs to be a factor (because the Traditions can't be objectively wrong); but that can't be all there is to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>XD<br /> <br /> FINALLY, a valid reason to make Technocracy to be Trump supporters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Too bad that no mage truly believe that reality it's subjective...they will insist in solving it with their Instruments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr />I can see your points, and I admit that having Nephandi preaching about the danger of climate change it's weird as shit<br /> <br /> However, I have to say, I find weird you believe that the Technocracy doesn't think that reality is Consensual. If anything, I believe the Technocracy it's more dependant of a Consensual Reality than the Traditions are. After all, they're the ones that spend billons trying to control the consensus.<br /> <br /> The whole thing it's built uppon things like &quot;you have to define reality&quot;, &quot;shove out of reality what we don't want&quot;, &quot;hide the truth to the masses untill it's gone&quot;. NWO Paradigm (Information it's Reality) will come appart if subjectivity isn't a thing. The Time Table it's based on the idea of making the masses accept a product so it can be part of the Consensus...and so and so. Paradox it's not just &quot;bad&quot;, it's against the law. Technocracy it's the more Consensus aware faction in the game.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:41:36-07:00","id":1106319,"title":"","content":"FWIW, my main objection to the Technocracy as it was portrayed in <b>Guide to the Technocracy</b> was that they were divided into two groups: those who knew that their objective reality propaganda was a lie, and those who didn't. With the latter almost entirely being victims of Conditioning by the former. What you describe is closer to how I like to handle the Union: they don't deny that there are subjective elements of reality; but they argue that there are rules by which people influence reality, that there's a \u201cnatural state of reality\u201d that the Awakened can either warp or reinforce, and that reinforcing this natural state ultimately leads to a more robust reality. Naturally, they're the ones who are trying to identify this natural state and then reinforce it. That is, they see Technocratic Reality as an extension of the Earthly Foundations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T17:40:02-07:00","id":1106342,"title":"","content":"I see. Then I misinterpreted your post.<br /> <br /> I think that's a cool way to make it. If at least some parts of the Technocracy weren't subjective, the Antrophic Paradigm would have no place and the Syndicate agent's won't have excuse to shut down an experiment on the grounds of it being too Utopical. But, at the same time, believing that there are objective foundations justifies Technocrats researching and believing in their discoveries.<br /> <br /> Really, I don't think most Traditionalists believe in an entirely subjective reality either. I mean, try to tell the average Chorister that God it's a human creation<br /> <br /> Besides, right now, anything that saves us from having nephandy hidden as climate change activists sounds golden to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:18:45-07:00","id":1106375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106342#post1106342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Then I misinterpreted your post.<br /> <br /> I think that's a cool way to make it. If at least some parts of the Technocracy weren't subjective, the Antrophic Paradigm would have no place and the Syndicate agent's won't have excuse to shut down an experiment on the grounds of it being too Utopical. But, at the same time, believing that there are objective foundations justifies Technocrats researching and believing in their discoveries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well\u2026 believing that there are objective foundations doesn't mean that you believe that what's bit on those foundations is necessarily objective. My interpretation of the Technocracy is that they believe in One Reality as an ideal to work toward, and their belief in objective foundations gives credence to their view that theirs is the right vision of what that one reality should be. However, they don't always agree, even among themselves, what that end goal should be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106342#post1106342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, I don't think most Traditionalists believe in an entirely subjective reality either. I mean, try to tell the average Chorister that God it's a human creation</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention that. It was the Choristers' view of the One that l was thinking of when I mentioned my aversion to saying that whatever is in Eternity is necessarily human. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106342#post1106342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, right now, anything that saves us from having Nephandi hidden as climate change activists sounds golden to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> My view on that is to look at Paradox, which I generally view as Unintended Consequences. That, and Earthly Foundations, which at its course is basically a declaration that the Consensus and Reality are two different things. Because the Consensus and Reality are two different things, the Consensus can suffer Paradox. <br /> <br /> Climate Change is the Consensus suffering Paradox.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:19:11-07:00","id":1106377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106287#post1106287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speak for yourself. Or are you \u201cNo True Scotsman\u201ding me, in that I'm not really a fan of Ascension because I have my doubts about purely subjective reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>It took me a few minutes to figure out what you thought I was saying. No, that comment was a correction for Aya. For some reason they assumed I was speaking about people who think the real world is subjective. In fact I was just talking about the people who prefer that Mage have a subjective reality.<br /> <br /> It's not my place to say who is and is not a fan, and I certainly wouldn't draw the line over subjective reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Real-world metaphysics inform Mage metaphysics. The former are a valid topic as long as you keep that in mind. </div> </div> </div>Completely valid, but in the context of a thread about Mage Metaphysics we should assume that the conversation is about Mage Metaphysics unless someone makes it clear they mean otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do like Aleph's notion of a temporal counterpart to the Correspondence Point, something that exists outside of Time and defines the rules of time without being subject to them. I'm not necessarily going to say that whatever it is that imposes its Will on Time is human. That's certainly a possibility; but in keeping with my preference for subjective reality only being subjectively true, I'm not in favor of nailing down the identity of whatever inhabits Eternity. </div> </div> </div>Keeping things flexible gets my vote as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 06-21-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T22:24:39-07:00","id":1106421,"title":"","content":"To <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> <br /> You will not find me saying otherwise in the way this is not my definition of subjective reality. Correct me, but I do not think subjective reality could be interpreted as subjective facts or, like the advisors of Mr trump call it &quot;alternative facts&quot;. I think subjective reality refer to the Laws of the Tellurian being subjective. I don't think anyone argue the facts, however they can argue the cause. Climate change is not subjective. It exists (you will always find people saying it does not, but that does not make their statement true, even in the WoD ^^). However, the causes for it are subject to debate. Is it the will of God? Is it caused by human activity? Is it the normal cycle of the Earth? Is it an angry court of Spirits? That's why reality is subjective. And reality zones argue that locally, the laws of the tellurian can adapt to people's belief.<br /> <br /> Subjective reality do not argue on the facts but on the causes. Well, that's the way I understand it anyway.<br /> <br /> Am I mistaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T03:59:28-07:00","id":1106471,"title":"","content":"I think both are viable terms of subjective reality.<br /> <br /> This is a usual complication, two factions use the same words with different meanings.<br /> <br /> Take Global Ascension, one term myriads of interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T04:50:14-07:00","id":1106487,"title":"","content":"Absolutely true!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:10:55-07:00","id":1106493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106287#post1106287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My go-to example is Climate Change: if reality really is determined by the Consensus, then a valid strategy for combatting Climate Change would be to convince the Masses that it doesn't exist. Perversely, those who warn of the danger and convince people that it's a real problem would be the ones responsible for it. So it can't be as simple as \u201creality is whatever you believe it is\u201d: belief, and will, needs to be a factor (because the Traditions can't be objectively wrong); but that can't be all there is to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it bad that some of my Technocrats actually believe this to be the case? Pollution, Global warming.. all of that is, much like carsickness, an invention of the traditions that spread.<br /> <br /> These things didn't cause problems until those meddling old folk convinced people they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:56:16-07:00","id":1106506,"title":"","content":"I would not say it's bad. I would say that the Technocracy knows better. However, may be they have an interest to make people believe this is nonsense. Economical or political reasons could do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:00:59-07:00","id":1106508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106493#post1106493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it bad that some of my Technocrats actually believe this to be the case? Pollution, Global warming.. all of that is, much like carsickness, an invention of the traditions that spread.<br /> <br /> These things didn't cause problems until those meddling old folk convinced people they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a number of ways of spinning this issue depending on if I want to make the Technocracy or the Traditions look like bad guys. My favorite way, though, is that the Traditions are trying to stop Climate Change by convincing the world it doesn't exist and that science is fallible, and the Technocracy is trying to stop Climate Change by convincing the world that it does exist but that we can stop it. They're both fighting to stop it, but they're getting in each other's way. As for who started it, I don't think either side knows. Manipulating the Consensus is more an art than a science.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:31:10-07:00","id":1106515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106508#post1106508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a number of ways of spinning this issue depending on if I want to make the Technocracy or the Traditions look like bad guys. My favorite way, though, is that the Traditions are trying to stop Climate Change by convincing the world it doesn't exist and that science is fallible, and the Technocracy is trying to stop Climate Change by convincing the world that it does exist but that we can stop it. They're both fighting to stop it, but they're getting in each other's way. As for who started it, I don't think either side knows. Manipulating the Consensus is more an art than a science.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why would Traditionalists want people to believe it does not exist? That will not make it disappear... It's like trying to make people believe man can fly. You can try if you have several centuries ahead of you. Laws of physics are part of the Consensus for way too long to think that changing the Consensus that way is a solution. That's either hubris, madness or one way trip to Ascension if you succeed ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:59:14-07:00","id":1106532,"title":"","content":"To the extent that Climate Change exists because people believe that it exists, promoting Denial of Climate Change should be effective in combatting it. But if you go with the notion that Climate Change is an unintended consequence of modern human activity \u2014 that it came about as a result of the Consensus, but not deliberately so \u2014 then refusing to believe in it will not make it go away. <br /> <br /> That's what I was getting at when I suggested that you might think of it as a sort of Paradox backlash against the Consensus: Paradox means that not everything brought about by the Consensus is deliberate. And you can't just wish away Paradox.<br /> <br /> Put another way: one of the conceits of Mage is that modern technology only works because the Consensus says it does. But modern technology that damages the environment doesn't do so because there's a faction out there that <i>wants</i> it to damage the environment; it's because Magick has a nasty tendency to do things people don't want it to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:23:06-07:00","id":1106536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106515#post1106515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would Traditionalists want people to believe it does not exist? That will not make it disappear... It's like trying to make people believe man can fly. You can try if you have several centuries ahead of you. Laws of physics are part of the Consensus for way too long to think that changing the Consensus that way is a solution. That's either hubris, madness or one way trip to Ascension if you succeed ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Falling off of cliffs has been a known quantity for thousands of years. Climate Change is a considerably younger concept. One is based on very visible principles that we start learning from the day we are born. The other is based on the interactions of chaotic systems that don't factor into the day to day life of most people. <br /> <br /> This is one of those things where plausibility depends a great deal on how you look at Subjective Reality. From what you said earlier it looks like you think of the physical laws of Mage as largely fixed, so largely invisible things like the behavior of neutrinos would be just as difficult to change as very visible things such as friction. I prefer to think that why things work is in flux so long as the world largely looks the same from day to day.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:32:45-07:00","id":1106538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106532#post1106532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you go with the notion that Climate Change is an unintended consequence of modern human activity \u2014 that it came about as a result of the Consensus, but not deliberately so \u2014 then refusing to believe in it will not make it go away.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one part of your argument I'm not getting. Why does how it came about change how belief affects it? Even if it turns out to be an unanticipated combination of several other principles, once you name it the Consensus should be able to affect it. Sure there's some inertial there, but it's not like beliefs with inertia haven't been overridden before.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:02:31-07:00","id":1106548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it bad that some of my Technocrats actually believe this to be the case? Pollution, Global warming.. all of that is, much like carsickness, an invention of the traditions that spread.<br /> <br /> These things didn't cause problems until those meddling old folk convinced people they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. My problem comes when acting like a carebear it's a valid strategy to destroy the world. As long as that doesn't happen we're ok.<br /> <br /> I want to elaborate on how I think mages think:<br /> <br /> I can see some NWO thinking that way, because they're the ones changing history books with the belief that this changes the past, or at least the relationship betwen the past and the present.<br /> <br /> But I can't see most Technocrats thinking like that. Among other things because climate change generated a whole new brand of technological development. Nowdays green industry it's growing, many new technologies are being buit with this in mind and I can't believe the Technocracy it's going to leave all that in the hands of the Society of Ether . Being green it's great marketing, making the Syndicate happy, and I guess they can manipulate ItX to include that in their new designs.<br /> <br /> I can see Verbena taking advantage of Climate Change to attack the Technocracy (See, we told you technology it's evil!), but I think that few mages relate to the Consensus as something that can be employed to solve problems directly, by itself (NWO being, probably, the biggest proponents of the idea).<br /> <br /> I think most Mages see the Consensus in a very limited way. They know magick it's easier where people believes, and harder where people don't. They know about Paradox, and while they don't know it's nature, they know it has something to do with the masses lack of faith.<br /> Some Technocrats may be forced by heavy Conditioning into thinking that Paradox it's just a flaw in the design of an experimental gadget, but I would think that agents expected to survive in the street (or expected to build gadgets that won't blow up when used in the street) have to know that local belief has an effect on what science can be used.<br /> But, all of this doesn't mean that they believe the universe it's ruled by belief. Most mages believe in greater forces, or have a perfectly logical explanation of natural phenomena that doesn't involve belief. Belief has power that an inteligent mage will harness, but you don't pray to people to stop the apocalipse, you pray to (or harness) a greater powers with the help of people and their belief.<br /> <br /> There are exeptions, like some VE that really have interiorized the Antrophic principle, or Etherites that really dig on all that Wall of Troy thing, some NWO agents that really opperate on &quot;mind/knowledge creates reality&quot;, some Syndicate agents that think there's no problem big enough that good marketing can't solve...etc. But I think that most mages don't opperate like that<br /> <br /> Finally, right now it's probably easier to convince people that climate change isn't anything dire, and that it can be solved with science, than to convince them it doesn't exist. After that, you can cast a Coincident spell (or various) to solve it, and, as bonus point, science get's to be the hero of the day.<br /> <br /> Traditions trying to convince people climate change doesn't exist...I can see an Archmaster opperating this way (and probably vanishing climate change with magick far before the Consensus vanishes it, as soon as casting the spell it's Coincident enough), but it think most Traditionalists are genuinely superstitious, and superstitious people ain't going to engineer social manipulation on that scale to solve what most of them likely perceive as &quot;god/s are angry with us&quot;, &quot;people has lost it's touch with nature/spirits/divine law and now we're paying the price&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-22-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:21:48-07:00","id":1106565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106548#post1106548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most Mages see the Consensus in a very limited way. They know magick it's easier where people believes, and harder where people don't. They know about Paradox, and while they don't know it's nature, they know it has something to do with the masses lack of faith.<br /> Some Technocrats may be forced by heavy Conditioning into thinking that Paradox it's just a flaw in the design of an experimental gadget, but I would think that agents expected to survive in the street (or expected to build gadgets that won't blow up when used in the street) have to know that local belief has an effect on what science can be used.<br /> But, all of this doesn't mean that they believe the universe it's ruled by belief. Most mages believe in greater forces, or have a perfectly logical explanation of natural phenomena that doesn't involve belief. Belief has power that an inteligent mage will harness, but you don't pray to people to stop the apocalipse, you pray to (or harness) a greater powers with the help of people and their belief</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or, in other words, all the Mages that actually believe in-game that the whole of reality is shaped by human beliefs, also would as a direct consequence have the Purple Paradigm. Which just isn't the case; The vast majority don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:34:03-07:00","id":1106572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106548#post1106548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most Mages see the Consensus in a very limited way. They know magick it's easier where people believes, and harder where people don't. They know about Paradox, and while they don't know it's nature, they know it has something to do with the masses lack of faith.<br /> Some Technocrats may be forced by heavy Conditioning into thinking that Paradox it's just a flaw in the design of an experimental gadget, but I would think that agents expected to survive in the street (or expected to build gadgets that won't blow up when used in the street) have to know that local belief has an effect on what science can be used.<br /> But, all of this doesn't mean that they believe the universe it's ruled by belief. Most mages believe in greater forces, or have a perfectly logical explanation of natural phenomena that doesn't involve belief. Belief has power that an inteligent mage will harness, but you don't pray to people to stop the apocalipse, you pray to (or harness) a greater powers with the help of people and their belief.<br /> <br /> There are exeptions, like some VE that really have interiorized the Antrophic principle, or Etherites that really dig on all that Wall of Troy thing, some NWO agents that really opperate on &quot;mind/knowledge creates reality&quot;, some Syndicate agents that think there's no problem big enough that good marketing can't solve...etc. But I think that most mages don't opperate like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is broadly what I think is going on with the Consensus and Mages. At this point most Mages know conceptually that belief changes reality, but the details of how it works are vague. That's why they focus more on distributing their beliefs and ideas and hope the rest takes care of itself. Even the NWO aren't masters of controlling the Consensus, they just have a lot more hands on experience at disseminating ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:36:04-07:00","id":1106697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106536#post1106536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falling off of cliffs has been a known quantity for thousands of years. Climate Change is a considerably younger concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I counted only a few centuries to change it that way ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106536#post1106536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One is based on very visible principles that we start learning from the day we are born. The other is based on the interactions of chaotic systems that don't factor into the day to day life of most people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaotic systems that don't factor into the day to day life of most poeple ? Well, now you're talking paradigm and causes. Not results of the climat changes, which can be visible by anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106536#post1106536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of those things where plausibility depends a great deal on how you look at Subjective Reality. From what you said earlier it looks like you think of the physical laws of Mage as largely fixed, so largely invisible things like the behavior of neutrinos would be just as difficult to change as very visible things such as friction. I prefer to think that why things work is in flux so long as the world largely looks the same from day to day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not consider the physical laws to be fixed. I could not play Mage if I did. I consider that the Consensus observes some facts and <i>considers</i> them true. The causes behind the facts are hidden and let to interpretation. Some will say Climate Change is caused by chaotic systems while others will only see the Hand of God and others will see the work of powerful spirits. Often, it is a bit of each. Well, did you ever wonder why Cyclones were named ? Some would say it is fancy, others will see a way to put it on equal ground with humanity and finally, some will say that these are the Cyclone spirit True Names ^^ Oh, Vengeful Katrina, why did you destroy everything on your Path to New-Orleans ?<br /> <br /> Neutrinos is science and I share that paradigm but well, who can say &quot;I saw them once !&quot; Not many... ? Not any ?<br /> <br /> What I grant you is that the limit between Facts and Paradigm oriented views is vague at least, and probably totally invisble. In that, I join you again, this is why I like the reality of the WoD to be somewhat... flexible. What I meant is that even if the concept of Climat Change is quite new, it is deeply rooted in poeple's minds. Discrediting the reality of Climat Change today may be more complicated than making poeple believe man can fly almost on his own (thanks to personal tech of course). I really do not think that the Traditions will try it. Nowadays, the Technocracy affiliated does much more propaganda against Climate Change the Traditionalists (not sure if I'm still speaking about Mage now...). Verbena, Ba'ta or Dreamskpears will surely try to fight Climate Change by direct actions. After all, to the Technocracy they're ecological terrorists aren't they ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:55:24-07:00","id":1106780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106697#post1106697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chaotic systems that don't factor into the day to day life of most poeple ? Well, now you're talking paradigm and causes. Not results of the climat changes, which can be visible by anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heat waves and collapsing ice shelves, no matter how visible they may be, simply are not as noticeable as something we notice with every moment and rely on with every step. That isn't a dig against Climate Change evidence its simply a statement of just how much we notice gravity. In general, if you don't learn it until school it isn't as deep as gravity, inertia, mass, or any of the other things you have to start figuring out to even move effectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not consider the physical laws to be fixed. I could not play Mage if I did. I consider that the Consensus observes some facts and <i>considers</i> them true. The causes behind the facts are hidden and let to interpretation. Some will say Climate Change is caused by chaotic systems while others will only see the Hand of God and others will see the work of powerful spirits. Often, it is a bit of each. Well, did you ever wonder why Cyclones were named ? Some would say it is fancy, others will see a way to put it on equal ground with humanity and finally, some will say that these are the Cyclone spirit True Names ^^ Oh, Vengeful Katrina, why did you destroy everything on your Path to New-Orleans ?<br /> <br /> Neutrinos is science and I share that paradigm but well, who can say &quot;I saw them once !&quot; Not many... ? Not any ? </div> </div> </div>Sounds like we are closer in view than I thought. Keep in mind, though, that I am comfortable taking Subjective reality far enough that the four humours were once a real thing and electrons were once not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I grant you is that the limit between Facts and Paradigm oriented views is vague at least, and probably totally invisble. In that, I join you again, this is why I like the reality of the WoD to be somewhat... flexible. What I meant is that even if the concept of Climat Change is quite new, it is deeply rooted in poeple's minds. Discrediting the reality of Climat Change today may be more complicated than making poeple believe man can fly almost on his own (thanks to personal tech of course). I really do not think that the Traditions will try it. Nowadays, the Technocracy affiliated does much more propaganda against Climate Change the Traditionalists (not sure if I'm still speaking about Mage now...). Verbena, Ba'ta or Dreamskpears will surely try to fight Climate Change by direct actions. After all, to the Technocracy they're ecological terrorists aren't they ? </div> </div> </div>In my experience Climate Change isn't rooted that deep, but as with all politically charged issues you have to go with what works at the gaming table. Interesting idea about the Technocracy trying to disprove Climate Change, though. I... actually could see that. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:32:48-07:00","id":1107074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like we are closer in view than I thought. Keep in mind, though, that I am comfortable taking Subjective reality far enough that the four humours were once a real thing and electrons were once not.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you need to use instruments to confirm the existence of something (such as electrons), it's possible that that thing is merely a figment of your Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T05:36:44-07:00","id":1107985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1107074#post1107074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you need to use instruments to confirm the existence of something (such as electrons), it's possible that that thing is merely a figment of your Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that explanation stolen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:17:48-07:00","id":1108141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1107074#post1107074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you need to use instruments to confirm the existence of something (such as electrons), it's possible that that thing is merely a figment of your Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, Mage: The Ascension is a setting where Confirmation Bias isn't just a feature of psychology, but a natural phenomenon inherent to Reality itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:50:41-07:00","id":1108156,"title":"","content":"Kinda. Bear in mind, though, that one of the forms of Quiet is all about taking Confirmation Bias to an extreme. \u201cDenial\u201d is a better name for it than \u201cClarity\u201d; but it still doesn't quite capture it's essence: someone in Denial has something that he believes in so much that he literally can't see things that contradict it. \u201cDenial\u201d puts the emphasis on what you're rejecting, where the emphasis really ought to be on what you're rejecting it <i>for</i>: what's sacred to you, what's beyond questioning? That's where confirmation bias really comes into its own. Technocrats as soulless agents of conformity are emblematic of this form of Quiet; but they're hardly the only ones.<br /> <br /> Conversely, your paradigm can have consequences that surprise you; and if you can keep an open mind (stay out of Denial), these surprises can enrich your paradigm and lead to new insights and new possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-26-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:34:45-07:00","id":1144057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1106126#post1106126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm...the One and the Pure Ones (Mage-from the very first edition and never leaved) would like to disagree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problematic and inconsistent themes, especially that are never broached in game play (when will a PC meet a Pure One?) can be safely ignored for table play. The IC fiction and OOC notes consistently refer to Mage as a subjective reality setting that is based *soley* on belief. Mage 20 and it's reality zones confirm this. If you want an objective reality Wizard game, Mage The Awakening 2E is really awesome and you should try it. But canonically, belief (even the belief of the Pure Ones if you use that setting element) drives -all- reality in Mage The Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:53:05-07:00","id":1144065,"title":"","content":"One of M20's \u201cReality Zones\u201d is the Earthly Foundations: things that are Vulgar regardless of belief (and, by implication, things that are Coincidental regardless of belief). To say that Mage is a subjective reality setting that is based solely on belief is to oversimplify Mage; it has more depth than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:13:01-07:00","id":1144074,"title":"","content":"Exactly, my coment was to higlight that there is OOC stuff to argue that reality may not be <i>entirely </i>subjective. <i>&quot;Human belief changes reality&quot; </i>it's a basic assumption in Mage, but <i>&quot;belief IS reality and nothing can be real without belief&quot;/&quot;belief CREATED reality, there was nothing before human belief&quot;/&quot;belief it's THE ONLY FORCE that changes or influences reality&quot;</i> /<i>&quot;the Consensus it's omnipotent, nothing falls outside it's reach&quot; are</i> all very debatable and ultimately subject to interpretation. Mage universe being subjective it's just an interpretation that bases itself on the premises of mage, but it's not the only interpretation that's been supported by the bible<br /> <br /> You can easily ignore in table many subjective elements of mage: How can characters discover if the Eartly Foundations were set by Gaia or just are things ingrained in human mind?, How can characters know if the Spheres were discovered or invented?, How can characters know if vampires are immune to Paradox because a higher being gave them this immunity instead of being &quot;part of the human subconscious&quot;? (what an utter bullshit that, vampires are part of the human subcoscious but dragons arent't?, bullshit). How can they know that reality dind't existed before humans had belief?<br /> <br /> This has it's uses. For instance, having a certain level of scepticism about the reach of the Consensus helps when you do crossover and do not want other supernatural powers to be subject to Zones, or when you want to introduce misteries about the nature of avatars, Prime, and other esoteric stuff that you want to exist regardless of Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-26-2017, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T09:15:05-07:00","id":1144097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1105543-could-i-get-some-people-to-poke-holes-in-my-head-canon?p=1144057#post1144057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problematic and inconsistent themes, especially that are never broached in game play (when will a PC meet a Pure One?) can be safely ignored for table play. The IC fiction and OOC notes consistently refer to Mage as a subjective reality setting that is based *soley* on belief. Mage 20 and it's reality zones confirm this. If you want an objective reality Wizard game, Mage The Awakening 2E is really awesome and you should try it. But canonically, belief (even the belief of the Pure Ones if you use that setting element) drives -all- reality in Mage The Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that the time before humans is largely irrelevant unless your story specifically calls for it, but I have to agree with the others on the rest. As much as I am a massive proponent of Consensus Determines All, it is far from the only way of interpreting Mage. There's quite a bit of play in the way subjective reality is described so it's precise meaning is open to debate. <br /> <br /> Also, while Belief is Reality seems straightforward, there are actually a couple of pitfalls you have to navigate before it really matches the world Mage describes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}